      "writtenOn": "2025-02-04T23:24:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why add `const` everywhere?\n\nit doesn\u0027t matter much either way IMO, but this all went through API review, so it shouldn\u0027t be changed without a good reason\n\ni see that the rust code switched to using shared refs intead of exclusive refs. we don\u0027t necessarily want to make a promise about that in a stable ABI like this + the pointer qualifiers aren\u0027t directly connected to the rust ref semantics, they don\u0027t really need to match. `const*` is never good enough by itself to assume that taking a shared ref is OK",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 337,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 337,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "41f273cf6cb577478ece24b5d67dfba9fc453120",
